---
code: K0028
title: Bad Record Update
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, record-update]
description: "Record update entry after '|' is empty or malformed"
---

A record update expression (`{ target | path: value, ... }`) must list at least one field update entry after `|`, where each entry is a field path followed by `:`, `+=`, `-=`, `*=`, `/=`, or `%=` and a value expression.

## Example

This error occurs when the update list after `|` is empty, uses `=`, or omits a field path:

```kura
let empty-update = { user | }

let bad-op = { user | name = "Tazz" }
```

## Solution

Provide at least one valid `path: value` or compound update (`+=`, `-=`, `*=`, `/=`, `%=`) entry after `|`:

```kura
let updated-user = { user | name: "Tazz", login-count += 1 }
```
